emória.", "q6": "O EGC é gratuito?", "a6": "Sim. O motor é Apache-2.0 e continua gratuito. Se um dia houver algo pago, será uma camada para equipes por cima do motor, nunca a memória na sua máquina.", "q7": "A biblioteca de prompts é obrigatória?", "a7": "Não. Ela é opcional e vem desligada por padrão: o instalador pergunta, e o motor (memória e Guardian) funciona do mesmo jeito sem ela.", "cl.title": "<span>Mesmo projeto.</span> <em>Nova sessão.</em>", "cl.gh": "Ver no GitHub", "com.title": "Feito por um desenvolvedor, mantido em aberto.", "com.support": "O EGC é gratuito. Se ele economiza seu tempo, apoie o projeto.", "com.sponsors": "GitHub Sponsors", "com.paypal": "Doar via PayPal", "com.partner": "Parceiro de ferramenta", "com.backer": "Apoiador", "com.gh": "Código, issues e releases", "com.npm": "Pacote @egchq/egc", "com.discord": "Comunidade e suporte", "com.hf": "Vitrine para a comunidade de IA", "ft.tag": "Extended Global Context. Memória persistente para ferramentas de IA, entre sessões e ferramentas.", "ft.docs": "Documentação", "ft.project": "Projeto", "ft.security": "Segurança", "ft.guide": "Guia de instalação", "ft.memory": "Memória", "ft.mcp": "Servidores MCP", "ft.arch": "Arquitetura", "ft.int": "Integrações", "ft.releases": "Releases", "ft.issues": "Issues", "ft.contrib": "Como contribuir", "ft.vision": "Visão", "ft.hof": "Hall of Fame", "ft.rss": "RSS de releases", "ft.policy": "Política de segurança", "ft.adv": "Security Advisories", "ft.dep": "Dependency Review", "ft.privacy": "Privacidade", "ft.license": "Publicado sob a <a href=\"https://github.com/Fmarzochi/EGC/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">licença Apache 2.0</a>. © 2026 <a href=\"https://github.com/Fmarzochi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Felipe Marzochi</a>.", "ld.faq": "{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"inLanguage\": \"pt-BR\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"O EGC envia os dados do meu projeto para algum lugar?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Não. Todo o estado fica salvo localmente em ~/.egc. Nada é enviado para servidores externos: os servidores MCP se comunicam por stdio apenas com a ferramenta de IA da sua máquina.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Quais ferramentas são compatíveis?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"21 ferramentas: Claude Code, Cursor, Codex CLI, Antigravity, OpenCode, Devin Desktop, Amp, VS Code Copilot, Zed, Kiro, Trae, CodeBuddy, JetBrains Junie, Goose, OpenHands, Aider, Warp, Cline, Qwen Code, Kimi Code CLI e Crush. O instalador detecta automaticamente quais estão na sua máquina.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Preciso pedir para a IA carregar o contexto?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Não. O egc install escreve o protocolo de memória no arquivo de instruções global de cada ferramenta, e a IA é orientada a carregar o estado no início de cada sessão. Em versões de ferramentas que não leem esse arquivo automaticamente, pode ser preciso adicioná-lo ao contexto manualmente.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Qual a diferença para um CLAUDE.md ou .cursorrules?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Esses arquivos são estáticos e versionados no repositório. O estado do EGC é dinâmico e local: a IA escreve nele a cada sessão, acumulando decisões e preferências. Os dois se complementam.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Funciona com vários projetos?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Sim. O estado é guardado por projeto e por branch do git. Cada projeto tem sua própria memória.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"O EGC é gratuito?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Sim. O motor é Apache-2.0 e continua gratuito. Se um dia houver algo pago, será uma camada para equipes por cima do motor, nunca a memória na sua máquina.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"A biblioteca de prompts é obrigatória?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Não. Ela é opcional e vem desligada por padrão: o instalador pergunta, e o motor (memória e Guardian) funciona do mesmo jeito sem ela.\"}}]}"}, "en": {"meta.title": "EGC — Context that never resets · persistent memory for AI coding tools", "meta.desc": "EGC is a local-first, open-source runtime that gives the 21 AI coding tools on your machine the same project memory, in every session.", "a.skip": "Skip to content", "a.home": "EGC, home page", "a.navMain": "Main", "a.navMobile": "Mobile menu", "a.menuOpen": "Open menu", "a.menuClose": "Close menu", "a.lang": "Language", "a.langPt": "Portuguese (Brazil)", "a.langEn": "English", "a.gh": "EGC repository on GitHub (opens in a new tab)", "a.copyInstall": "Copy install command", "a.copyTab": "Copy the commands from the selected tab", "a.newTab": "(opens in a new tab)", "ui.copy": "copy", "ui.copyCmds": "copy commands", "ui.copied": "copied", "ui.copyFail": "select and copy", "ui.copiedMsg": "Commands copied to the clipboard.", "ui.copyFailMsg": "Could not copy automatically. Select the text and copy it.", "ui.langChanged": "Language changed to English.", "nav.demo": "Demo", "nav.features": "Features", "nav.integrations": "Integrations", "nav.install": "Install", "nav.docs": "Docs", "nav.cta": "Install", "hero.eyebrow": "New session?", "hero.l1": "Context", "hero.l2": "that never <em>resets.</em>", "hero.copy": "EGC gives the AI tools on your machine <strong>the same project memory</strong>. Decisions, preferences and next steps come back in every session, in any tool.", "hero.ctaInstall": "Install EGC", "hero.ctaDemo": "See it work", "hero.meta": "Release details", "hero.m.local": "100% local", "hero.m.tools": "21 tools", "hero.markCap": "4 faculties · 1 local engine", "ben.eyebrow": "The problem", "ben.title": "Why start over <em>every time?</em>", "ben.lede": "Close the window and the context is gone: your stack preferences, last week’s architecture decisions, the approach that failed after three attempts. Switch from Cursor to Claude Code and you start over again.", "ben.voicesLabel": "What you repeat every session without EGC", "ben.you": "you ›", "ben.v1": "We use PostgreSQL with row-level security…", "ben.v2": "I prefer functional components, no classes…", "ben.v3": "We moved from Prisma to Drizzle because…", "ben.figcap": "Illustrative comparison: without EGC, the context available to the AI drops to zero at every new session; with EGC it is restored and builds up across sessions.", "ben.col0": "context", "ben.col1": "session 1", "ben.col2": "session 2", "ben.col3": "session 3", "ben.without": "Without EGC", "ben.withoutSub": "resets every session", "ben.with": "With EGC", "ben.withSub": "restores and builds up", "ben.tagReexplain": "↺ re-explain", "ben.chartNote": "illustrative chart · not to scale", "ben.chartOk": "&gt; egc restore — context ready", "ben.w1": "Repeating context in every session", "ben.w2": "Losing important decisions", "ben.w3": "Re-explaining project structure", "ben.c1": "Context restored in every new session", "ben.c2": "Decisions kept with the project", "ben.c3": "Switch tools, keep going", "demo.eyebrow": "Demo", "demo.title": "One decision, <em>two tools.</em>", "demo.lede": "Follow one decision: recorded in Cursor, kept by EGC and restored in Claude Code, without you repeating anything.", "demo.badge": "Illustrative demo", "demo.badgeNote": "A simulated interface that explains the flow. Not a real recording.", "demo.controls": "Demo controls", "demo.play": "Play", "demo.pause": "Pause", "demo.restart": "Restart", "demo.stepsLabel": "Demo steps", "demo.goStep": "Go to step", "demo.s1": "The session records a decision", "demo.s2": "The session is closed", "demo.s3": "Another tool is opened", "demo.s4": "EGC restores the decision", "demo.s5": "Work continues", "demo.d1": "In Cursor you decide to switch ORMs. The AI saves the decision with <code>store_decision</code>.", "demo.d2": "You close the window. The decision stays encrypted in <code>~/.egc</code>, on your machine.", "demo.d3": "Days later you open Claude Code on the same project and just say “let’s continue”.", "demo.d4": "EGC loads the project state and hands the decision to the new session.", "demo.d5": "The AI picks up where you left off, already knowing what was decided.", "demo.winA": "Cursor · session 1", "demo.winB": "Claude Code · session 2", "demo.closed": "session closed", "demo.waiting": "waiting for a new session…", "demo.uA1": "Let’s move off Prisma and use Drizzle. Keep that.", "demo.aiA1": "Decision recorded for this project and branch.", "demo.card": "Decision", "demo.cardBody": "ORM: Prisma → Drizzle", "demo.vault": "local memory", "demo.vaultNote": "AES-256-GCM · per project and branch", "demo.uB1": "let’s continue", "demo.restored": "context restored", "demo.aiB1": "I know the ORM is now Drizzle. Continuing the schema migration with it.", "demo.live0": "Demo paused.", "demo.liveStep": "Step", "demo.of": "of", "demo.reduced": "Reduced motion is on: step through with the buttons.", "fx.eyebrow": "How it works", "fx.title": "One brain, <em>four faculties.</em>", "fx.lede": "One local engine, on from the first install in every supported tool. Each circle in the mark is one of the parts working together for you.", "fx.details": "Technical details", "fx.example": "Visual example", "f1.name": "Memory", "f1.title": "What one agent learns, every agent knows.", "f1.short": "Decisions and lessons are kept and come back in any tool.", "f1.body": "Decisions, session context, working memory and learned lessons are captured as you work and are available in any terminal, IDE or agent. You speak naturally, in any language: “save this session”, “what did we decide about auth?”. There is no command to memorize.", "f1.proof": "<b>get_state</b> · <b>update_state</b> · <b>store_decision</b> · <b>search_history</b> · <b>lesson_save</b> — per project and per branch", "f1.link": "How memory works", "f1.v.save": "save", "f1.v.restore": "restore", "f2.name": "Session Mesh", "f2.title": "Your open sessions see each other.", "f2.short": "Parallel sessions announce what they’re on and cooperate instead of colliding.", "f2.body": "Two Cursor tabs, a Claude Code terminal and an Antigravity session share one live bus. They announce what they are working on, claim the files they edit and hand work to each other.", "f2.proof": "<b>session_announce</b> · <b>claim_path</b> · <b>session_send</b> · <b>session_wait</b> — events delivered exactly once", "f2.link": "See the MCP servers", "f2.v.claim": "claimed", "f2.v.wait": "waits", "f3.name": "Guardian", "f3.title": "Safety before every command.", "f3.short": "Risky commands and writes are checked before they run, in the background.", "f3.body": "Guardian validates commands before they run, gates risky writes and keeps context from overflowing, without you invoking anything.", "f3.caveat": "Caveat: coverage depends on each tool’s own hook support. The exceptions are documented in the project’s security assessment.", "f3.proof": "<b>validate_command</b> blocks shell injection · <b>validate_write</b> protects paths like ~/.ssh and /etc · <b>validate_content</b> flags prompt injection (advisory only)", "f3.link": "Meet Guardian", "f3.v.blocked": "blocked", "f3.v.allowed": "allowed", "f4.name": "Token Crusher", "f4.title": "Noise never reaches the model.", "f4.short": "Long shell output is compressed by up to 90%, keeping errors and warnings.", "f4.body": "Before shell output reaches the model, Token Crusher compresses git logs, test spam, install noise and giant JSON while keeping every error and warning. Ask “how much did I save?” and the answer comes from your local ledger.", "f4.proof": "One <b>637 KB git log</b> became <b>31 KB</b> in a single crush · <b>egc gain</b> shows your own savings", "f4.link": "Read about token optimization", "f4.v.before": "before", "f4.v.after": "after", "f4.v.kept": "errors kept", "int.eyebrow": "Integrations", "int.title": "Works with the tools <em>you already use.</em>", "int.lede": "<code>egc install</code> detects what is installed and sets up each tool with what it can read.", "int.devTitle": "Coding tools", "int.provTitle": "Model providers", "int.provLede": "Bring your own model. Works natively with these providers, plus OpenRouter as a broker.", "int.showAll": "See all integrations", "int.showLess": "Show less", "int.allSite": "Integrations page", "int.hint": "Select a tool to see its support type.", "int.support": "Support type", "int.core": "Core-supported", "int.community": "Community-supported", "int.coreNote": "Run daily by the maintainer or a steward; a regression caused by a vendor change is fixed before the next release.", "int.communityNote": "Installed and tested in CI like the rest; a vendor change waits for a report or a pull request.", "int.page": "Integration page", "int.native": "native", "int.broker": "broker", "int.k.MCP": "MCP: the local memory and Guardian servers are registered in the tool.", "int.k.Skills": "Skills: guides and procedures the tool reads.", "int.k.Hooks": "Hooks: hooks that run Guardian before actions.", "int.k.Bootstrap": "Bootstrap: the memory protocol is written into the tool’s instructions.", "int.k.Context": "Context: a context file the tool loads.", "int.k.Plugin": "Plugin: integration through the tool’s plugin system.", "int.k.Guidelines": "Guidelines: guidelines in the format the tool reads.", "int.k.Rules": "Rules: rules in the format the tool reads.", "eff.eyebrow": "Efficiency", "eff.cap": "fewer tokens to rebuild context every session.", "eff.estimate": "EGC project estimates", "eff.without": "without EGC", "eff.with": "with EGC", "eff.m1": "Context overhead per session", "eff.m1a": "~1,500 tokens", "eff.m1b": "~200 tokens", "eff.m2": "Time re-explaining the project", "eff.m2a": "10 min/session", "eff.m2b": "0", "eff.m3": "Cost for 20 sessions per month", "eff.m3a": "~$0.08–0.09", "eff.m3b": "~$0.011–0.012", "eff.m4": "Shell output sent to the model", "eff.m4a": "full output", "eff.m4b": "up to 90% smaller", "eff.note": "Bars are proportional to the figures published by the project (ranges at their midpoint). Run <code>egc gain</code> to see the savings recorded on your machine.", "prv.eyebrow": "Privacy & security", "prv.title": "Your memory lives <em>on your machine.</em>", "prv.k1": "Local-first", "prv.v1": "Nothing leaves your computer.", "prv.s1": "The MCP servers talk over stdio only to your local AI tool.", "prv.k2": "Encryption", "prv.v2": "AES-256-GCM at rest.", "prv.s2": "GCM authentication detects corruption on read.", "prv.k3": "Scope", "prv.v3": "Per project and per branch.", "prv.s3": "Switching branches restores that branch’s context.", "prv.k4": "Repository", "prv.v4": "Never committed to git.", "prv.s4": "Memory stays out of your source code.", "prv.k5": "License", "prv.v5": "Open source, Apache-2.0.", "prv.s5": "The engine stays free.", "prv.proofs": "Public security checks", "prv.model": "Security model", "ins.eyebrow": "Install", "ins.title": "Two commands. <em>No step three.</em>", "ins.st1": "Install the package", "ins.st1p": "Requires Node.js 20 or later. Works on Windows, macOS and Linux.", "ins.st2": "Run <code>egc install</code>", "ins.st2p": "Detects your tools, registers the local MCP servers and writes the memory protocol. It only asks whether you want the optional prompt library.", "ins.st3": "Just talk", "ins.st3p": "Open your tool and say “let’s continue”. Memory loads on its own.", "ins.tabs": "Install method", "ins.rec": "recommended", "ins.npmNote": "Linux, macOS and Windows. No git clone needed.", "ins.req": "Requires <a href=\"https://nodejs.org/en/download\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Node.js 20+</a> and git.", "ins.reqWin": "Requires <a href=\"https://nodejs.org/en/download\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Node.js 20+</a> and PowerShell.", "ins.verify": "# verify", "ins.guide": "Full installation guide", "faq.eyebrow": "FAQ", "faq.title": "Frequently asked <em>questions.</em>", "faq.more": "Didn’t find what you were looking for?", "faq.link": "See the full FAQ", "q1": "Does EGC send my project data anywhere?", "a1": "No. All state is stored locally in ~/.egc. Nothing is sent to external servers: the MCP servers talk over stdio only to the AI tool on your machine.", "q2": "Which tools are supported?", "a2": "21 tools: Claude Code, Cursor, Codex CLI, Antigravity, OpenCode, Devin Desktop, Amp, VS Code Copilot, Zed, Kiro, Trae, CodeBuddy, JetBrains Junie, Goose, OpenHands, Aider, Warp, Cline, Qwen Code, Kimi Code CLI and Crush. The installer auto-detects which ones you have.", "q3": "Do I need to ask the AI to load context?", "a3": "No. egc install writes the memory protocol into each tool’s global instruction file, and the AI is told to load state at the start of every session. For tool versions that don’t read that file automatically, you may need to add it to the session context manually.", "q4": "How is this different from a CLAUDE.md or .cursorrules file?", "a4": "Those files are static and committed to the repo. EGC state is dynamic and project-local: the AI writes to it every session, building up decisions and preferences. They complement each other.", "q5": "Does it work with multiple projects?", "a5": "Yes. State is stored per project and per git branch. Each project gets its own memory.", "q6": "Is EGC free?", "a6": "Yes. The engine is Apache-2.0 and stays free. If EGC ever offers something paid, it will be a team layer on top of the engine, never the memory on your machine.", "q7": "Is the prompt library required?", "a7": "No. It is optional and off by default: the installer asks, and the engine (memory and Guardian) works the same without it.", "cl.title": "<span>Same project.</span> <em>New session.</em>", "cl.gh": "View on GitHub", "com.title": "Built by one developer, maintained in the open.", "com.support": "EGC is free. If it saves you time, support the project.", "com.sponsors": "GitHub Sponsors", "com.paypal": "Donate via PayPal", "com.partner": "Tool partner", "com.backer": "Backer", "com.gh": "Code, issues and releases", "com.npm": "Package @egchq/egc", "com.discord": "Community and support", "com.hf": "Showcase for the AI community", "ft.tag": "Extended Global Context. Persistent memory for AI tools, across sessions and tools.", "ft.docs": "Docs", "ft.project": "Project", "ft.security": "Security", "ft.guide": "Installation guide", "ft.memory": "Memory", "ft.mcp": "MCP servers", "ft.arch": "Architecture", "ft.int": "Integrations", "ft.releases": "Releases", "ft.issues": "Issues", "ft.contrib": "Contributing", "ft.vision": "Vision", "ft.hof": "Hall of Fame", "ft.rss": "Releases RSS", "ft.policy": "Security policy", "ft.adv": "Security Advisories", "ft.dep": "Dependency Review", "ft.privacy": "Privacy", "ft.license": "Released under the <a href=\"https://github.com/Fmarzochi/EGC/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apache 2.0 License</a>. © 2026 <a href=\"https://github.com/Fmarzochi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Felipe Marzochi</a>.", "ld.faq": "{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"inLanguage\": \"en\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Does EGC send my project data anywhere?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"No. All state is stored locally in ~/.egc. Nothing is sent to external servers: the MCP servers talk over stdio only to the AI tool on your machine.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Which tools are supported?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"21 tools: Claude Code, Cursor, Codex CLI, Antigravity, OpenCode, Devin Desktop, Amp, VS Code Copilot, Zed, Kiro, Trae, CodeBuddy, JetBrains Junie, Goose, OpenHands, Aider, Warp, Cline, Qwen Code, Kimi Code CLI and Crush. The installer auto-detects which ones you have.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Do I need to ask the AI to load context?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"No. egc install writes the memory protocol into each tool’s global instruction file, and the AI is told to load state at the start of every session. For tool versions that don’t read that file automatically, you may need to add it to the session context manually.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How is this different from a CLAUDE.md or .cursorrules file?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Those files are static and committed to the repo. EGC state is dynamic and project-local: the AI writes to it every session, building up decisions and preferences. They complement each other.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Does it work with multiple projects?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes. State is stored per project and per git branch. Each project gets its own memory.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Is EGC free?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes. The engine is Apache-2.0 and stays free. If EGC ever offers something paid, it will be a team layer on top of the engine, never the memory on your machine.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Is the prompt library required?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"No. It is optional and off by default: the installer asks, and the engine (memory and Guardian) works the same without it.\"}}]}"}}; window.EGC_TOOLS = [{"name": "Claude Code", "slug": "claude-code", "badge": "MCP + Skills", "icon": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,", "core": true}, {"name": "Cursor", "slug": "cursor", "badge": "MCP + Bootstrap", "icon": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,", "core": true}, {"name": "Codex CLI", "slug": "codex-cli", "badge": "MCP + Skills", "icon": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,", "core": true}, {"name": "Antigravity", "slug": "antigravity", "badge": "MCP + 